id: pm-web-qihk
title: Migrate hand-written public/sw.js and public/cookie-consent.js to TypeScript sources
description: "Migrate the hand-written public/sw.js service worker and public/cookie-consent.js classic script to TypeScript sources only, with deterministic build outputs emitted at the same public URLs (/sw.js, /cookie-consent.js). Add ServiceWorker + DOM typings with no any/ts-ignore, remove hand-written JS source status (make them generated build artifacts), retain the generated JS at the public URLs for runtime packaging, integrate with build/typecheck/watch/release/pack scripts, update tests to validate source and generated behavior, keep HTML behavior unchanged. Do not touch HTML/CSS source, hosted data, telemetry, Caddy, secrets, or legal text."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: pm-web-i98h-child,static-runtime,typescript-sources
created_at: "2026-07-13T05:09:11.928Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-13T05:55:20.730Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-13T05:43:19.243Z"
author: pi-pm-web-typescript
acceptance_criteria: "public/sw.js and public/cookie-consent.js are generated from TypeScript sources (no hand-written JS source); output is valid JS (no TS type annotations) served at the same public URLs /sw.js and /cookie-consent.js; ServiceWorker and DOM typings are added with zero any/@ts-ignore; npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm test, npm run audit:prod, npm run pack:dry-run, and npm run changelog:check all pass; tests validate source typing and generated output behavior; HTML/CSS source, hosted data, telemetry, Caddy, secrets, and legal text are untouched"
parent: pm-web-i98h
risk: high
confidence: high
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T05:27:16.748Z",pi-pm-web-typescript,"Resolution & evidence (2026-07-13): PROBLEM: npm run release:check failed at audit:prod with EALLOWSCRIPTS (--allow-scripts not allowed in project-scoped installs) because ~/.npmrc sets allow-scripts and the bare `npm audit --omit=dev` inherited the restricted environment. The partial migration also introduced `npx tsc` in typecheck:frontend/build:frontend, which can trigger npx network resolution even though local tsc exists. FIX (package.json only; no HTML/CSS/legal/hosted/telemetry/secrets touched): (1) audit:prod changed from `npm audit --omit=dev` to `env -u npm_config_allow_scripts npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts` (matches established pattern in pm-csv/pm-github/pm-linear; unsets npm_config_allow_scripts so npm does not reject the restricted environment, --ignore-scripts keeps audit non-mutating). (2) typecheck:frontend/build:frontend replaced all `npx tsc` with bare `tsc` (npm adds node_modules/.bin to PATH; local typescript@7.0.2 resolves with no npx/network fallback) and extended to compile the three frontend projects (main + tsconfig.sw.json + tsconfig.scripts.json). VERIFICATION (all green): git diff check shows only .gitignore/package.json/public/tsconfig.json changed plus pre-existing .agents/pm files preserved; untracked TS sources + tsconfigs + test. npm run typecheck PASS. npm run build PASS. npm test 74 pass 0 fail (incl 4 new static-scripts tests). Direct audit: env -u npm_config_allow_scripts npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts found 0 vulnerabilities exit 0. Scripted audit: npm run audit:prod found 0 vulnerabilities exit 0 (EALLOWSCRIPTS resolved). npm run pack:dry-run PASS (207 files; public/sw.js 12.4kB + public/cookie-consent.js 2.1kB packed for runtime serving). npm run changelog:check: Changelog up to date exit 0. npm run release:check (full gate) exit 0. Generated outputs public/sw.js + public/cookie-consent.js are valid plain JS (new Function parses), serve exactly at /sw.js and /cookie-consent.js, and are git-ignored (.gitignore lines 15-16); public/src/sw.ts and public/src/cookie-consent.ts are tracked (NOT ignored). ACTUAL RESULT: all acceptance criteria met."
  "2026-07-13T05:43:11.927Z",codex-root,"Reopened-item follow-up — Greptile bb239654 P2 findings addressed minimally (2 source files only; no HTML/CSS/legal/hosted/telemetry/secrets/Greptile/unrelated files touched; not committed/pushed):\n\n1) public/tsconfig.scripts.json (import-free directly-served cookie-consent classic script): removed the bundler-specific \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\", letting TypeScript 7 apply its direct-script default. Verified TS 7 context: \"classic\", \"node\"/\"node10\" are REMOVED (TS5108); \"node16\"/\"nodenext\" require matching module values (TS5110); only \"bundler\" or the omitted default are valid with module:ES2022, so omitting is the correct TS-7-compatible direct-script default. Strictness NOT weakened: \"strict\": true preserved (tsc --showConfig confirms strict:true, moduleResolution no longer present). moduleDetection:\"legacy\" retained (classic-script-appropriate, not bundler-specific). cookie-consent.ts typecheck+emit green; emitted /cookie-consent.js (2130 bytes) still parses as plain JS classic IIFE.\n\n2) test/static-scripts.test.ts buildScripts() helper: changed execFileSync stdio from [\"ignore\",\"pipe\",\"pipe\"] (captures diagnostics) to [\"ignore\",\"inherit\",\"inherit\"] — tsc stdout/stderr diagnostics now forward directly to the CI log while stdin stays ignored (noninteractive, no prompts). On tsc failure, diagnostics flow to CI instead of being trapped in the thrown error.\n\nVERIFICATION (pm test --run --progress, all green):\n- linked-test 1/3 audit:prod (env -u npm_config_allow_scripts npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts): passed exit 0, 0 vulnerabilities.\n- linked-test 2/3 npm run release:check: passed exit 0 — typecheck + build + 74/74 tests pass 0 fail (incl 4 static-scripts tests using the modified buildScripts helper) + audit:prod 0 vuln + pack:dry-run 207 files (public/sw.js 12.4kB + public/cookie-consent.js 2.1kB packed) + changelog:check up to date.\n- linked-test 3/3 npm run typecheck:frontend: passed exit 0.\n\ngit diff scope: only public/tsconfig.scripts.json (-1 line) and test/static-scripts.test.ts (+2/-1) changed."
  "2026-07-13T05:55:20.724Z",codex-root,"CI follow-up 2026-07-13: GitHub Actions run 29227244124 failed only changelog:check because the newly closed item was absent from CHANGELOG.md. Fetched full tags, ran npm run changelog:full, and reproduced CI's full --mode replace --all-release-tags check locally; now green. TypeScript/test/audit gates were unaffected."
files[5]{path,scope,note}:
  .gitignore,project,public/sw.js and public/cookie-consent.js ignored as generated build artifacts served at the same public URLs
  package.json,project,"audit:prod made environment-neutral (env -u npm_config_allow_scripts npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts); npx tsc replaced with bare local tsc to avoid npx network resolution; typecheck:frontend/build:frontend extended to compile sw.ts + cookie-consent.ts via tsconfig.sw.json/tsconfig.scripts.json"
  public/src/cookie-consent.ts,project,"TypeScript source for /cookie-consent.js (DOM lib, classic IIFE, no any/ts-ignore)"
  public/src/sw.ts,project,"TypeScript source for /sw.js (WebWorker lib, no any/ts-ignore)"
  test/static-scripts.test.ts,project,"validates TS sources tracked, generated JS ignored+valid+URLs, precache covers all chunks"
tests[3]{command,scope}:
  env -u npm_config_allow_scripts npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts,project
  "npm run release:check",project
  "npm run typecheck:frontend",project
close_reason: "Greptile bb239654 P2 findings addressed minimally: (1) removed bundler-specific moduleResolution from the import-free directly-served cookie-consent classic-script tsconfig (public/tsconfig.scripts.json) using the TS7-compatible direct-script default without weakening strictness (strict:true preserved); (2) buildScripts() in test/static-scripts.test.ts now forwards tsc stdout/stderr diagnostics to CI via stdio ['ignore','inherit','inherit'] while remaining noninteractive. Full release:check green (typecheck+build+74/74 tests+audit:prod 0 vuln+pack:dry-run 207 files+changelog:check). 2 source files changed; nothing committed/pushed; no unrelated/Greptile/HTML/CSS/legal/hosted/secrets files touched."
body: ""
